{
  "version": 1,
  "source_hash": 15787693145197822512,
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Spinlock and raw_spinlock",
      "source_hash": 9092238966781000614,
      "context_hash": 15160548572211440205,
      "translation": "스핀락과 raw_spinlock",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856390Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Busy-wait locks that don't sleep — the foundation of kernel synchronization",
      "source_hash": 14502250538837368887,
      "context_hash": 6950111130944185916,
      "translation": "슬립하지 않는 busy-wait 락 — 커널 동기화의 기반",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856391Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "What is a spinlock?",
      "source_hash": 15461477687262091536,
      "context_hash": 5794772352479412544,
      "translation": "스핀락이란 무엇인가",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856392Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "A spinlock is a lock that a thread holds by spinning in a tight loop until the lock becomes available.",
      "source_hash": 12937567670435569722,
      "context_hash": 1638193596619335786,
      "translation": "스핀락은 락을 사용할 수 있게 될 때까지 스레드가 촘촘한 루프를 돌며 스핀하여 획득하는 락입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856392Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Unlike a mutex, it never puts the thread to sleep.",
      "source_hash": 16217186282257004840,
      "context_hash": 6912044213207041481,
      "translation": "뮤텍스와 달리 스레드를 절대 슬립시키지 않습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "mutex": "뮤텍스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856392Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:2",
      "source": "This makes spinlocks usable in contexts where sleeping is forbidden — interrupt handlers, NMI handlers, and anywhere `in_interrupt()` is true.",
      "source_hash": 3857344267004004792,
      "context_hash": 18416622678065529168,
      "translation": "따라서 스핀락은 슬립이 금지된 컨텍스트, 즉 인터럽트 핸들러, NMI 핸들러, 그리고 `in_interrupt()`가 참인 모든 곳에서 사용할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "handlers": "핸들러",
        "interrupt handlers": "인터럽트 핸들러",
        "spinlocks": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856392Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "The cost: spinning wastes CPU cycles.",
      "source_hash": 4143674048779078101,
      "context_hash": 5624204094427209643,
      "translation": "대가: 스핀은 CPU 사이클을 낭비합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856393Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:1",
      "source": "Spinlocks should only protect very short critical sections (typically microseconds, not milliseconds).",
      "source_hash": 13479487472096315887,
      "context_hash": 18229648498498669501,
      "translation": "스핀락은 매우 짧은 임계 구역(critical section)만 보호해야 합니다(보통 밀리초가 아닌 마이크로초 단위).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "critical sections": "임계 구역",
        "spinlocks": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856393Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Two spinlock types",
      "source_hash": 17628631262497889780,
      "context_hash": 3124098572242623806,
      "translation": "두 가지 스핀락 타입",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856393Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The kernel has two types that look similar but behave differently on PREEMPT_RT kernels:",
      "source_hash": 496252358968117450,
      "context_hash": 17416569356867027465,
      "translation": "커널에는 겉보기에는 비슷하지만 PREEMPT_RT 커널에서 다르게 동작하는 두 가지 타입이 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널",
        "kernels": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856393Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "On a standard kernel (non-RT), `spinlock_t` and `raw_spinlock_t` behave identically.",
      "source_hash": 11785853509622559450,
      "context_hash": 7429125519632798561,
      "translation": "표준 커널(non-RT)에서는 `spinlock_t`와 `raw_spinlock_t`가 동일하게 동작합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "On a PREEMPT_RT kernel, `spinlock_t` becomes a sleeping lock (backed by `rt_mutex`) so that RT tasks can preempt the lock holder. `raw_spinlock_t` remains a true spinlock even on RT.",
      "source_hash": 12821823531979079804,
      "context_hash": 6456739959203332936,
      "translation": "PREEMPT_RT 커널에서는 RT 태스크가 락 보유자를 선점할 수 있도록 `spinlock_t`가 (`rt_mutex` 기반의) 슬립하는 락이 됩니다. `raw_spinlock_t`는 RT에서도 진정한 스핀락으로 남습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RT tasks": "RT 태스크",
        "kernel": "커널",
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "**Rule**: use `spinlock_t` for most code.",
      "source_hash": 6620822808496542107,
      "context_hash": 15085581265630733998,
      "translation": "**규칙**: 대부분의 코드에서는 `spinlock_t`를 사용하십시오.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:5/seg:1",
      "source": "Use `raw_spinlock_t` only when you need a true spinlock even on RT kernels (e.g., the scheduler's runqueue lock, which cannot sleep because the scheduler itself is how sleeping works).",
      "source_hash": 6510854089596870283,
      "context_hash": 13101229252549264071,
      "translation": "RT 커널에서도 진정한 스핀락이 필요한 경우에만 `raw_spinlock_t`를 사용하십시오(예: 스케줄러의 런큐 락은 스케줄러 자체가 슬립을 구현하는 주체이므로 슬립할 수 없습니다).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernels": "커널",
        "runqueue": "런큐",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러",
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Basic API",
      "source_hash": 17857012803577255832,
      "context_hash": 3919740081016883317,
      "translation": "기본 API",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "API": "API"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "When to use irqsave vs plain spin_lock",
      "source_hash": 6008566448371532033,
      "context_hash": 7426653252597696470,
      "translation": "irqsave와 일반 spin_lock의 사용 시점",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The rule: you need `spin_lock_irqsave()` if the same lock is acquired from both process context and an interrupt handler.",
      "source_hash": 10972397171912477832,
      "context_hash": 3132717842298356431,
      "translation": "규칙: 같은 락을 프로세스 컨텍스트와 인터럽트 핸들러 양쪽에서 획득한다면 `spin_lock_irqsave()`가 필요합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "interrupt handler": "인터럽트 핸들러",
        "process": "프로세스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "If the lock is only used within a single IRQ handler (or only in process context where IRQs are already off), plain `spin_lock()` is sufficient.",
      "source_hash": 4175078123326348324,
      "context_hash": 6374203870272621272,
      "translation": "락이 단일 IRQ 핸들러 안에서만 사용되거나 IRQ가 이미 꺼진 프로세스 컨텍스트에서만 사용된다면 일반 `spin_lock()`으로 충분합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "IRQ": "IRQ",
        "IRQs": "IRQ",
        "handler": "핸들러",
        "process": "프로세스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "How it works: queued spinlocks",
      "source_hash": 17544843045763676784,
      "context_hash": 17857923845473791818,
      "translation": "동작 원리: queued 스핀락",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "spinlocks": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Modern x86 uses **queued spinlocks** (MCS-based, introduced in Linux 4.2 by Waiman Long — [`a33fda35e3a7`](https://git.kernel.org/linus/a33fda35e3a7655fb7df756ed67822afb5ed5e8d), [LWN](https://lwn.net/Articles/590243/)).",
      "source_hash": 15209729537654228008,
      "context_hash": 11008806827847551947,
      "translation": "최신 x86은 **queued 스핀락**(MCS 기반, Waiman Long이 Linux 4.2에서 도입 — [`a33fda35e3a7`](https://git.kernel.org/linus/a33fda35e3a7655fb7df756ed67822afb5ed5e8d), [LWN](https://lwn.net/Articles/590243/))을 사용합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "LWN": "LWN",
        "Linux": "Linux",
        "spinlocks": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Instead of all waiters spinning on the same variable (causing cache line bouncing), each CPU spins on its own per-CPU node:",
      "source_hash": 16523598973544534860,
      "context_hash": 10607254940779227587,
      "translation": "모든 대기자가 같은 변수에서 스핀하는(캐시 라인 바운싱을 유발하는) 대신, 각 CPU는 자신의 per-CPU 노드에서 스핀합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU",
        "cache": "캐시",
        "node": "노드"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "When a CPU acquires the lock it clears `locked` in the next CPU's node, causing only that waiter to stop spinning.",
      "source_hash": 6183832740947750004,
      "context_hash": 12949472219899786626,
      "translation": "CPU가 락을 획득하면 다음 CPU 노드의 `locked`를 지우며, 이로써 해당 대기자만 스핀을 멈춥니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU",
        "node": "노드"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:1",
      "source": "This scales to hundreds of CPUs.",
      "source_hash": 2051885313309039782,
      "context_hash": 12088353459158428383,
      "translation": "이 방식은 수백 개의 CPU까지 확장됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPUs": "CPU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:12.856396Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:0/seg:0",
